WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.826
Your agent says it's done. So the board says it's done. The board has never met a customer.

2
00:00:08.376 --> 00:00:15.697
The tests pass, on the machine that wrote them. The demo is real, at eight times speed.

3
00:00:15.697 --> 00:00:20.009
The testimonial comes from a very satisfied placeholder.

4
00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:24.110
Making got fast. Believing did not.

5
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:29.696
The gap between made and real has no owner, so it gets a launch week.

6
00:00:30.246 --> 00:00:33.413
A render has never failed a drop test.

7
00:00:33.963 --> 00:00:41.872
Everything is already conspiring to get you over the line: agents, tools, suppliers, testers.

8
00:00:41.872 --> 00:00:49.847
Product Actualizer pins the plot to one board. One model, every claim graded, every lens reading it.

9
00:00:50.397 --> 00:00:59.318
Says who? Trust me. On the real unit? On the render. Who decides it's done? Whatever did the work.

10
00:00:59.318 --> 00:01:03.196
Here the answers are a source, a gate, and you.

11
00:01:03.746 --> 00:01:12.219
Even the agent cannot accept its own work. It tried. The cockpit declined, in capital letters.

12
00:01:12.769 --> 00:01:17.618
Product Actualizer. Finish the product. Show the evidence.
